The A64 scalar saturating arithmetic and 64-bit vector min and max on the arm64 backend

Why: the arm64 backend left these emitters unimplemented (an abort when a block uses them).
CMHI and CMHS on 64-bit elements (the client runs them) become VectorMinU64 and VectorMaxU64;
the scalar SQADD, UQADD, SQSUB, UQSUB (B, H, S, D) and SQDMULH (H, S) are the
SignedSaturated*/UnsignedSaturated* opcodes. Each is the host's own instruction: CMGT or CMHI
with BSL for min and max, and the scalar saturating instruction with the guest's FPSR loaded,
so QC is set as on the device. emulator/src/cpu.rs's patched_emitters_agree_with_the_host runs
each through the JIT and on the host and compares.

Upstream: azahar-emu/dynarmic a46601580d55 (its master on 2026-11-12) lacks these; they are
not sent upstream.

